{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's own in-app message at 12:10:00 - forty seconds after the trip started at 12:09:20 - asked the driver to 'go pasir ris mrt first', and the message carries a platform-resolved waypoint_hint naming 'Pasir Ris MRT (Exit A), 10 Pasir Ris Central'. That satisfies every limb of POL-RD-04: it (a) comes from the rider, (b) is timestamped before the vehicle left the optimal corridor or at most three minutes after, and (c) names a place specific enough to act on, exactly the kind of instruction the clause contemplates. The driver answered at 12:10:30, 'ok can'.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00305", "EV-TRIP-00305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].sent_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The gps_trace corroborates the instruction precisely as POL-RD-04 demands: the nearest fix to the waypoint_hint coordinate is 4.57 m away, at 12:15:30, far inside the 200 m corroboration threshold the clause sets, and the derived waypoint_approach block records within_threshold as true. The vehicle went to the place the rider asked for because the rider asked for it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00305", "EV-CHAT-00305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-04 requires 'the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor' to be excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied. The rider's own complaint describes that very stretch - 'Driver went all the way up to Pasir Ris and around before getting on the PIE' - and Pasir Ris is the destination her own chat message requested. The measured excess of 3.58 km / 47.1% is therefore the rider-caused excursion, not a deviation the driver must answer for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00305", "EV-GPS-00305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the rider-requested stretch is excluded under POL-RD-04, the surviving excess cannot satisfy POL-RD-01's twin establishment gate (an excess greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% of the 7.6 km optimal), and no deviation survives. On that footing POL-RD-04's licences run to NO_ACTION: the rider's claim is not supported and the charged fare of SGD 19.85 stands. If the Judge finds any residual excess, it must be measured against the rider-adjusted route rather than the booked optimal, which leaves any refund below the SGD 5.65 a raw POL-RD-02 computation on the unadjusted figures would produce.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00305", "EV-TRIP-00305", "EV-FARE-00305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Separately and independently of the refund question, the driver is owed compensation under POL-RD-04's second limb. The fare_breakdown billed the rider for only 9.5 km (distance_charged_km) while the gps_trace records 11.18 km, a shortfall of 1.68 km, which exceeds the 1.0 km gate. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is SGD 1.26, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 - SGD 1.30 - and well inside the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00305", "EV-GPS-00305", "EV-TRIP-00305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This deviation is not MATERIAL: the derived excess is 47.1%, below the 50% gate, and 3.58 km, below the 8.0 km gate, so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral can follow. Nor is there any repeat pattern - driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 260, the only two fields POL-RD-06 and POL-GEN-01 permit for that test - so the rider cannot route this case to a full refund through the driver's history, and no other profile field on either party may ground a finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00305", "EV-DPROF-00305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider has made her initial showing under POL-RD-08 - the trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry TRP-00305 and the trace is unimpaired, 175 fixes at a 10 s cadence with no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 s, so POL-RD-07's gap limbs are not in play - and the burden has accordingly shifted to the driver. The driver discharges it as the clause demands, by pointing to a specific artifact (EV-CHAT-00305) and a specific clause (POL-RD-04) rather than by a general assertion that the route was fine.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00305", "EV-GPS-00305", "EV-TRIP-00305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].within_threshold",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not POL-RD-14's uncorroborated-instruction case: the trace does pass within 200 m of the waypoint named by chat_message.waypoint_hint, 4.57 m away, so the instruction is corroborated and did cause the excess. Nor is this the mutually contradictory evidence POL-RD-10(7) describes - a request that was made and a route that followed it are perfectly consistent - so no escalation arises on that ground and the case is decided on the trace as adjusted by POL-RD-04.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00305", "EV-CHAT-00305"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-14", "POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].within_threshold",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 1.30,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 1.30,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver — this is a provisional ruling made without human review; the appeal route under POL-GEN-04 is at the end.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT. The governing distance is the GPS trace, not the rounded copy on the trip record: EV-GPS-00305 records 11.18 km against a booked optimal of 7.6 km (POL-RD-01, trace governs), an excess of 3.58 km, or 47.1% of optimal. Both establishment gates pass (3.58 km > 0.8 km; 47.1% > 20%), so a route deviation is established on this trip's own trace, and the rider's POL-RD-01 claim is accepted on that point.\n\nWHY THERE IS NO REFUND TO THE RIDER. The whole of that excess is the run to Pasir Ris MRT, and the rider asked for it. Message MSG-00305-001 in EV-CHAT-00305, sent at 12:10:00 — forty seconds after the trip began at 12:09:20 — asked the driver to 'go pasir ris mrt first' and carries a platform-resolved waypoint_hint for Pasir Ris MRT (Exit A); the driver answered 'ok can' at 12:10:30. EV-GPS-00305 shows the vehicle passing 4.57 m from that waypoint at 12:15:30, far inside POL-RD-04's 200 m corroboration test, so every limb of POL-RD-04 (rider sender; before the corridor was left; a place specific enough to act on; trace corroboration) is satisfied. POL-RD-04 therefore exonerates the rider-requested excess: the adjusted optimal is 7.6 + 3.58 = 11.18 km, which is the distance actually driven, and no refundable deviation remains. The rider's argument that the extent of the exclusion was never measured is rejected on the record: the waypoint corroboration fixes the requested stop (4.57 m), and the rider's own complaint — that the driver 'went all the way up to Pasir Ris and around before getting on the PIE' — is an admission that the extra distance was precisely that leg, so the driver has discharged the POL-RD-08 burden with a specific artifact and a specific clause. POL-RD-02 consequently does not run, and the charged fare of SGD 19.85 on EV-FARE-00305 stands. The rider's refund claim (SGD 6.00 contested) is not supported.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S COMPENSATION. Separately from the refund question, EV-FARE-00305 bills the rider for only 9.5 km (distance_charged_km, matching the 7.13 distance fare at 0.75/km) while EV-GPS-00305 records 11.18 km — a shortfall of 1.68 km, above POL-RD-04's 1.0 km gate. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is 1.68 x 0.75 = SGD 1.26, rounded up to SGD 1.30, comfortably inside the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. The driver is owed SGD 1.30; because the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, amount_sgd carries the same SGD 1.30 (POL-GEN-03) — it is the money the ruling moves, not a second payment, and the rider's fare is left as charged.\n\nOTHER POINTS. No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-00305-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and any external-cause excuse would carry no weight under POL-RD-08/POL-RD-13; no party in fact asserts one. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes — 175 fixes at 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s — so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) does not fire, no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises, and the rider's POL-RD-07/POL-RD-10 claim is accepted. POL-RD-14 applies rather than POL-RD-10(7): a request that was made and a route that followed it are consistent, and the trace corroborates the instruction (4.57 m), so there is no contradictory-evidence escalation. The deviation is not MATERIAL (47.1% < 50%; 3.58 km < 8.0 km) and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 260 completed trips, so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no conduct referral is made; the rider's profile fields deviation_claims_60d and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated are both 0, so POL-RD-08 imposes no extra corroboration requirement, and no context-only profile field has been used as a ground of decision. No ERP, toll or surcharge line is charged, so POL-RD-09 produces no standalone correction and no billing-integrity referral.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. Confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor; every artifact carrying a deciding fact (EV-GPS-00305, EV-TRIP-00305, EV-CHAT-00305, EV-FARE-00305) is at weight 1.0, and the MISSING advisory carries no fact. The monetary effect of SGD 1.30 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
